# Copy to .env.local
#
# Option A — no key (default): the built-in static rubric grades every stage
# offline. Works out of the box, but feedback is checklist-style.
#
# Option B — server-wide key (all users get AI reviews):
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#
# Option C — local Ollama (free, no key, OpenAI-compatible):
# 1) ollama pull llama3.1 && ollama serve
# 2) LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#    LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible provider (OpenRouter, Groq, Together…) works via
# LLM_BASE_URL + LLM_MODEL. If the LLM call fails for any reason, the app
# silently falls back to the static rubric.
#
# Code execution (/api/run): by default runs on this host (python3/node/java
# toolchains, fresh temp dir, 10s timeout per stage). NEVER enable that on a
# public server — there local execution is refused unless you opt in AND you
# should prefer a sandboxed runner instead:
# ALLOW_LOCAL_RUN=1
# PISTON_API_URL=https://piston.example.com/api/v2/piston
# PISTON_API_KEY=... (only if your instance requires auth)
#
# Auth: local email + password accounts in SQLite (scrypt-hashed) — no env
# setup needed. Guests can use everything without an account; logged-in
# attempts are stamped with the account id (attempts.userId).
#
# Database: SQLite file by default (local dev + single-node deploys).
# Set DATABASE_URL for Postgres instead (serverless-safe):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/lld
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
